entry.summary:
We prove that a saturated weakly branch group $G$ has the property $R_\infty$ (any automorphism $φ:G\to G$ has infinite Reidemeister number) in each of the following cases:
  1) any element of $Out(G)$ has finite order;
  2) for any $φ$ the number of orbits on levels of the tree automorphism $t$ inducing $φ$ is uniformly bounded and $G$ is weakly stabilizer transitive;
  3) $G$ is finitely generated, prime-branching, and weakly stabilizer transitive with some non-abelian stabilizers (with no restrictions on automorphisms).
  Some related facts and generalizations are proved.
